IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`

-- PART 10 -- Appeals (regulations 93 to 100 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and
-- Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017, S.I. 2017/692, United Kingdom),
-- lines 2756-2853 of uksi-2017-692.txt.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.  The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter
-- script; it is not the official text, and nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER.  A decision function answers JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING.
-- JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words; each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (...)` with the quoted words.  NOTHING is "the text does not answer"; each such
-- branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Marginal readings, listed in NOTES.md: (a) a trailing "if" on a power, an "is"-definition and
-- a flat negative are the text's no; (b) a grant or a prohibition limited by its own wording is
-- not a no; (c) a "must" or a time limit that has not been met is the text's no.
-- Rulings of 2026-11-05, tagged `[ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]` and `[ruled 2026-11-05 (b) where]`
-- on the branch (they are not the marginal readings above): a period the text fixes in its own
-- words answers JUST FALSE outside it; a "where" condition that is not met answers JUST FALSE;
-- a scope limit with no "only" answers NOTHING outside the scope.
-- A duty function (a "must") answers JUST FALSE only for a breach.  Where the duty arises "if" or
-- "where" something holds, a companion function, `... the duty ... arises`, answers JUST FALSE when
-- it does not arise, and the duty function answers NOTHING then.
--
-- HOW A DAY IS COUNTED (fork F-PERIOD).  The text has no rule for counting days (the Interpretation
-- Act 1978 is outside the sources).  Every period below is a NUMBER of days after an anchor date,
-- where the anchor date itself is day 0.  "Within 30 days from the date" is read as ending on day
-- 30, because "from" leaves the anchor day out.  "A period of 30 days beginning with the date" is
-- read as ending on day 29, because "beginning with" counts the anchor day as the first.
-- A seam is marked `-- SEAM S-n (asking|answering)`.

§ `Part 10 -- Appeals`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- Decisions of the FCA`

§§ `Regulation 93 -- Appeals against decisions of the FCA`

-- Reg 93(1): a person may appeal to the Upper Tribunal a decision by the FCA under one of seven provisions.  The first three are decisions that other parts of the Regulations define (seam S-19).
-- src:2759 | (1) A person may appeal to the Upper Tribunal a decision by the FCA under—
-- src:2760 | (a) regulation 25(2), to issue a direction;
-- src:2761 | (b) regulation 59(1), to refuse to register an applicant;
-- src:2762 | (c) regulation 60, to suspend or cancel the registration of a registered person;
-- src:2763 | (ca) regulation 74C(1), to impose a direction;
-- src:2764 | (d) regulation 76, to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement;
-- src:2765 | (e) regulation 77, to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation;
-- src:2766 | (f) regulation 78(2), to impose a prohibition.
@ref reg 93(1) (src:2759-2766)
-- SEAM S-19 (asking)
GIVEN `the decision is made by the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 25(2) the decision is a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 59(1) the decision refuses to register an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 60 the decision suspends or cancels a registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 74C(1) to impose a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 77 to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(1) a person may appeal to the Upper Tribunal` IS
    IF `the decision is made by the FCA` AND (`reg 25(2) the decision is a direction` OR `reg 59(1) the decision refuses to register an applicant` OR `reg 60 the decision suspends or cancels a registration` OR `the decision is under regulation 74C(1) to impose a direction` OR `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` OR `the decision is under regulation 77 to take a measure set out in paragraph (2)(a) or (b) of that regulation` OR `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a decision by the FCA under— (a) regulation 25(2), to issue a direction; ..."

-- Reg 93(2): Part 9 of FSMA applies to these appeals as it applies to references under that Act, subject to the modifications in paragraph (3).  What Part 9 of FSMA says is outside the sources.
-- src:2767 | (2) The provisions of Part 9 of FSMA (hearings and appeals), apply, subject to the modifications set out in paragraph (3), in respect of appeals to the Upper Tribunal made under this regulation as they apply in respect of references made to that Tribunal under that Act.
@ref reg 93(2) (src:2767)
GIVEN `the appeal to the Upper Tribunal is made under this regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(2) Part 9 of FSMA applies to the appeal with the modifications in paragraph (3)` IS
    IF `the appeal to the Upper Tribunal is made under this regulation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what Part 9 of FSMA says is not in the sources

-- Reg 93(3)(a): in section 133(7A) of FSMA, after paragraph (o), a new paragraph (p).
-- src:2768 | (3) Part 9 of FSMA has effect as if—
-- src:2769 | (a) in section 133 (proceedings before Tribunal: general provision), in subsection (7A) , after paragraph (o) there were inserted—
-- src:2770 | (p) a decision to take action under any of regulations 76 to 78 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.
@ref reg 93(3) (src:2768-2770)
@ref reg 93(3)(a) (src:2768-2770)
GIVETH A STRING
`reg 93(3)(a) the paragraph inserted after paragraph (o) of section 133(7A) of FSMA` MEANS "(p) a decision to take action under any of regulations 76 to 78 of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017."

-- Reg 93(3)(b), the substituted section 133A(1): the action in a decision notice under regulation 81(6) must not be taken during the referral period, nor, if the matter is referred, until the reference and any appeal have been finally disposed of.  No bearer is named (the passive "must not be taken"), so no prohibition is derived.
-- src:2771 | (b) for section 133A there were substituted—
-- src:2772 | 133A Proceedings before Tribunal: decision notices
-- src:2773 | (1) The action specified in a decision notice given under regulation 81(6) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017 must not be taken—
-- src:2774 | (a) during the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal under the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017; and
-- src:2775 | (b) if the matter is so referred, until the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of.
@ref reg 93(3) the substituted section 133A(1) (src:2771-2775)
GIVEN `the decision notice was given under regulation 81(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been referred to the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(3)(b) section 133A(1) the action specified in the decision notice may be taken` IS
    IF `the decision notice was given under regulation 81(6)` AND (`the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal has not ended` OR (`the matter has been referred to the Tribunal` AND (NOT `the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of`)))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The action specified in a decision notice given under regulation 81(6) ... must not be taken— (a) during the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal ...; and (b) if the matter is so referred, until the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section says when the action must not be taken and nothing of when it may be
-- The same bar asked the other way round (ruled 2026-11-05 (d), a bar that lasts "until"): is the action still barred?  JUST TRUE inside the period and while the reference is pending, JUST FALSE once the bar has ended.  It never says the action may be taken: the section gives no permission (see the function above, which answers NOTHING after the bar).
@ref reg 93(3) the substituted section 133A(1) (src:2771-2775)
GIVEN `the decision notice was given under regulation 81(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter has been referred to the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(3)(b) section 133A(1) the action specified in the decision notice is barred` IS
    IF `the decision notice was given under regulation 81(6)`
    THEN IF `the period within which the matter to which the notice relates may be referred to the Tribunal has not ended` OR (`the matter has been referred to the Tribunal` AND (NOT `the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be taken— (a) during the period within which the matter ... may be referred to the Tribunal ...; and (b) if the matter is so referred, until the reference, and any appeal against the Tribunal's determination, has been finally disposed of" [ruled 2026-11-05 (d) bar]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The action specified in a decision notice given under regulation 81(6)"

-- Reg 93(3)(b), the substituted section 133A(2): the Tribunal may make recommendations about the FCA's regulating provisions or procedures.
-- src:2776 | (2) The Tribunal may, on determining a reference under these Regulations in respect of a decision of the FCA, make recommendations as to its regulating provisions or its procedures.
@ref reg 93(3) the substituted section 133A(2) (src:2776)
GIVEN `the Tribunal is determining a reference under these Regulations in respect of a decision of the FCA` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 93(3)(b) section 133A(2) the Tribunal may make recommendations as to the FCA's regulating provisions or procedures` IS
    IF `the Tribunal is determining a reference under these Regulations in respect of a decision of the FCA`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on determining a reference under these Regulations in respect of a decision of the FCA"

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Decisions of the Commissioners`

§§ `Regulation 94 -- Offer of review`

-- Reg 94(1): the Commissioners must offer a review of a decision notified to P if an appeal lies under this Chapter.
-- src:2779 | (1) The Commissioners must offer a person (“P”) a review of a decision that has been notified to P if an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision.
@ref reg 94(1) (src:2779)
GIVEN `the decision has been notified to P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94(1) the duty to offer P a review arises` IS
    IF `the decision has been notified to P` AND `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision" [marginal (a)]
@ref reg 94(1) (src:2779)
GIVEN `the decision has been notified to P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners offered P a review of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94(1) the Commissioners offered P a review` IS
    IF `the decision has been notified to P` AND `an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision`
    THEN IF `the Commissioners offered P a review of the decision`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioners must offer a person (“P”) a review of a decision that has been notified to P" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if an appeal lies under this Chapter in respect of the decision"; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 94(1) the duty to offer P a review arises`

-- Reg 94(2): the offer is made by notice given at the same time as the decision is notified.
-- src:2780 | (2) The offer of a review must be made by notice given to P at the same time as the decision is notified to P.
@ref reg 94(2) (src:2780)
GIVEN `the Commissioners make an offer of a review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer was made by notice given to P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given at the same time as the decision was notified to P` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94(2) the offer of a review was made by notice at the same time as the decision` IS
    IF `the Commissioners make an offer of a review`
    THEN IF `the offer was made by notice given to P` AND `the notice was given at the same time as the decision was notified to P`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The offer of a review must be made by notice given to P at the same time as the decision is notified to P" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- Reg 94(3): this regulation does not apply to the notification of the conclusions of a review.
-- src:2781 | (3) This regulation does not apply to the notification of the conclusions of a review.
@ref reg 94(3) (src:2781)
GIVEN `the notification is of the conclusions of a review` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 94 applies to the notification` IS
    IF `the notification is of the conclusions of a review`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation does not apply to the notification of the conclusions of a review" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

§§ `Regulation 95 -- Review by the Commissioners`

-- Reg 95(1): the Commissioners must review a decision if they offered a review and P notifies acceptance within 30 days from the date of the notice of the offer.  "From" leaves the notice day out (F-PERIOD): the last day is day 30.
-- src:2783 | (1) The Commissioners must review a decision if—
-- src:2784 | (a) they have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter, and
-- src:2785 | (b) the person concerned (“P”) notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer within 30 days from the date of the notice of the offer of a review.
@ref reg 95(1) (src:2783-2785)
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the date of the notice of the offer, as day 0, on which P notified acceptance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(1) the duty to review the decision arises` IS
    IF `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` AND `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` AND `the days after the date of the notice of the offer, as day 0, on which P notified acceptance` <= 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioners must review a decision if— (a) they have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter, and (b) the person concerned (“P”) notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer within 30 days from the date of the notice of the offer of a review" [ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]
@ref reg 95(1) (src:2783-2785)
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the date of the notice of the offer, as day 0, on which P notified acceptance` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioners reviewed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(1) the Commissioners reviewed the decision` IS
    IF `the Commissioners have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter` AND `P notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer` AND `the days after the date of the notice of the offer, as day 0, on which P notified acceptance` <= 30
    THEN IF `the Commissioners reviewed the decision`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioners must review a decision if— (a) they have offered a review of the decision under this Chapter, and (b) the person concerned (“P”) notifies the Commissioners that P accepts the offer within 30 days from the date of the notice of the offer of a review" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an acceptance after day 30 is not covered here; regulation 97 may reach it; the duty does not arise, so there is no answer here: ask `reg 95(1) the duty to review the decision arises`

-- Reg 95(2): P may not notify acceptance where P has already appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100.
-- src:2786 | (2) P may not notify acceptance of the offer where P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100.
@ref reg 95(2) (src:2786)
GIVEN `P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(2) P may notify acceptance of the offer` IS
    IF `P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "P may not notify acceptance of the offer where P has already appealed against the decision to the tribunal under regulation 100" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- The bearer is named (P), so the prohibition is derived from the answer above (ruling N2).
DECLARE `reg 95(2) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 95(2) P`

DECLARE `reg 95(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 95(2) P notifies acceptance of the offer`

@ref reg 95(2) (src:2786)
GIVEN `reg 95(2) P may notify acceptance of the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 95(2) party` `reg 95(2) action`
DECIDE `reg 95(2) the prohibition on P` IS
    IF `reg 95(2) P may notify acceptance of the offer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `reg 95(2) P`
         SHANT `reg 95(2) P notifies acceptance of the offer`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 95(2) P` BECAUSE "P notified acceptance of the offer although P had already appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100, which regulation 95(2) forbids"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Reg 95(3): the Commissioners must not review a decision if P has appealed.  The bearer is named, so the prohibition is derived below (ruling N2).
-- src:2787 | (3) The Commissioners must not review a decision if P has appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100 in respect of the decision.
@ref reg 95(3) (src:2787)
GIVEN `P has appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100 in respect of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 95(3) the Commissioners may review the decision` IS
    IF `P has appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100 in respect of the decision`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Commissioners must not review a decision if P has appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100 in respect of the decision" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

DECLARE `reg 95(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `reg 95(3) the Commissioners`

DECLARE `reg 95(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `reg 95(3) the Commissioners review the decision`

@ref reg 95(3) (src:2787)
GIVEN `reg 95(3) the Commissioners may review the decision` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reg 95(3) party` `reg 95(3) action`
DECIDE `reg 95(3) the prohibition on the Commissioners` IS
    IF `reg 95(3) the Commissioners may review the decision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN PARTY `reg 95(3) the Commissioners`
         SHANT `reg 95(3) the Commissioners review the decision`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `reg 95(3) the Commissioners` BECAUSE "the Commissioners reviewed a decision although P had appealed to the tribunal under regulation 100, which regulation 95(3) forbids"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Regulation 96 -- Extensions of time`

-- Reg 96(4): "relevant period" is the 30 days in regulation 95(1)(b) or, once notices have been given, the period as most recently extended.  The answer is the last day of the period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer.
-- src:2794 | (4) In this regulation, “relevant period” means—
-- src:2795 | (a) the period of 30 days referred to in regulation 95(1)(b); or
-- src:2796 | (b) in the case where one or more notices have already been given under paragraph (1) the period as extended (or as most recently extended) in accordance with paragraph (2).
@ref reg 96(4) (src:2794-2796)
GIVEN `the day from which the most recent extension runs, in days after the date of the notice of the offer` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 96(4) the relevant period ends on day` IS
    CONSIDER `the day from which the most recent extension runs, in days after the date of the notice of the offer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 30
    WHEN JUST d THEN d + 30

-- Reg 96(1): the Commissioners may, within the relevant period, notify P that it is extended.
-- src:2789 | (1) If under this Chapter the Commissioners have offered a person (“P”) a review of a decision the Commissioners may within the relevant period notify P that the relevant period is extended.
@ref reg 96(1) (src:2789)
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered P a review of a decision under this Chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which the Commissioners give the notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the last day of the relevant period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 96(1) the Commissioners may notify P that the relevant period is extended` IS
    IF `the Commissioners have offered P a review of a decision under this Chapter` AND `the days after the date of the notice of the offer on which the Commissioners give the notice` <= `the last day of the relevant period, in days after the date of the notice of the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If under this Chapter the Commissioners have offered a person (“P”) a review of a decision the Commissioners may within the relevant period notify P that the relevant period is extended" [ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]

-- Reg 96(2): when a notice is given the relevant period is extended to the end of 30 days from (a) the date of the notice or (b) any other date set out in the notice or a further notice.
-- src:2790 | (2) If notice is given, the relevant period is extended to the end of 30 days from—
-- src:2791 | (a) the date of the notice; or
-- src:2792 | (b) any other date set out in the notice or a further notice.
@ref reg 96(2) (src:2790-2792)
GIVEN `a notice is given under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day from which the extension runs, in days after the date of the notice of the offer (the date of the notice, or any other date set out in the notice)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 96(2) the relevant period is extended to the end of day` IS
    IF `a notice is given under paragraph (1)`
    THEN JUST (`the day from which the extension runs, in days after the date of the notice of the offer (the date of the notice, or any other date set out in the notice)` + 30)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If notice is given"

-- Reg 96(3): more than one notice may be given.
-- src:2793 | (3) More than one notice may be given under paragraph (1).
@ref reg 96(3) (src:2793)
GIVEN `the number of notices already given under paragraph (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 96(3) a further notice may be given` IS
    IF `the number of notices already given under paragraph (1)` >= 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "More than one notice may be given under paragraph (1)"; the first notice is given under paragraph (1) itself

§§ `Regulation 97 -- Review out of time`

-- Reg 97(1): this regulation applies if the Commissioners offered a review and P did not accept it within the time allowed.
-- src:2798 | (1) This regulation applies if—
-- src:2799 | (a) the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to a person (“P”); and
-- src:2800 | (b) P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2).
@ref reg 97(1) (src:2798-2800)
GIVEN `the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to P` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 97(1) this regulation applies` IS
    IF `the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to P` AND `P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This regulation applies if— (a) the Commissioners have offered a review of a decision under this Chapter to a person (“P”); and (b) P does not accept the offer within the time allowed under regulation 95(1)(b) or 96(2)" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 97(2): the Commissioners must review the decision if P asks after the time allowed, in writing, and the Commissioners are satisfied of the reasonable excuse and the absence of unreasonable delay.
-- src:2801 | (2) The Commissioners must review the decision if—
-- src:2802 | (a) after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time;
-- src:2803 | (b) the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed; and
-- src:2804 | (c) the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply.
@ref reg 97(2) (src:2801-2804)
GIVEN `reg 97(1) this regulation applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 97(2) the duty to review the decision out of time arises` IS
    IF (`reg 97(1) this regulation applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `after the time allowed, P notifies the Commissioners in writing requesting a review out of time` AND `the Commissioners are satisfied that P had a reasonable excuse for not accepting the offer of a review within the time allowed` AND `the Commissioners are satisfied that P made the request without unreasonable delay after the excuse had ceased to apply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
