§§ `Regulation 99 -- Appeals against decisions of the Commissioners`

-- Reg 99(1): a person may appeal to the tribunal if the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners under one of six provisions.  Four of them are decisions other parts define (seam S-19).  A trailing "if" on a power: marginal reading (a).
-- src:2825 | (1) A person may appeal to the tribunal in accordance with regulation 100 if the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners under—
-- src:2826 | (a) regulation 25(2), to issue a direction;
-- src:2827 | (b) regulation 58, to the effect that a person is not a fit and proper person (unless the decision is required by virtue of paragraph (3) of that regulation);
-- src:2828 | (c) regulation 59(1), to refuse to register an applicant;
-- src:2829 | (d) regulation 60, to suspend or cancel the registration of a registered person;
-- src:2830 | (e) regulation 76, to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement;
-- src:2831 | (f) regulation 78(2), to impose a prohibition.
@ref reg 99(1) (src:2825-2831)
-- SEAM S-19 (asking)
GIVEN `the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 25(2) the decision is a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 58 the decision is that a person is not a fit and proper person, other than one required by regulation 58(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 59(1) the decision refuses to register an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 60 the decision suspends or cancels a registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 99(1) a person may appeal to the tribunal in accordance with regulation 100` IS
    IF `the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners` AND (`reg 25(2) the decision is a direction` OR `reg 58 the decision is that a person is not a fit and proper person, other than one required by regulation 58(3)` OR `reg 59(1) the decision refuses to register an applicant` OR `reg 60 the decision suspends or cancels a registration` OR `the decision is under regulation 76 to impose a penalty or publish a censuring statement` OR `the decision is under regulation 78(2) to impose a prohibition`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may appeal to the tribunal in accordance with regulation 100 if the person is the subject of a decision by the Commissioners under—" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 99(2): Part 5 of the Value Added Tax Act 1994 applies, subject to paragraph (3).  What Part 5 says is outside the sources.
