-- Reg 99(4): the tribunal's powers on an appeal.
-- src:2834 | (4) The tribunal hearing an appeal under paragraph (1) has the power to—
-- src:2835 | (a) quash or vary any decision of the Commissioners, including the power to reduce any penalty to such amount (including nil) as the tribunal thinks appropriate; and
-- src:2836 | (b) substitute the tribunal's own decision for any decision quashed on appeal.
@ref reg 99(4) (src:2834-2836)
DECLARE `reg 99(4) power` IS ONE OF
    `reg 99(4)(a) quash or vary any decision of the Commissioners`
    `reg 99(4)(b) substitute the tribunal's own decision for any decision quashed on appeal`
    `reg 99(4) some other power`

@ref reg 99(4) (src:2834-2836)
GIVEN `the tribunal is hearing an appeal under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      what IS A `reg 99(4) power`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 99(4) the tribunal has the power to` IS
    IF `the tribunal is hearing an appeal under paragraph (1)`
    THEN CONSIDER what
         WHEN `reg 99(4)(a) quash or vary any decision of the Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 99(4)(b) substitute the tribunal's own decision for any decision quashed on appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `reg 99(4) some other power` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the items are listed and the text does not say others are barred
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is for the tribunal hearing an appeal under paragraph (1)

@ref reg 99(4)(a) (src:2835)
GIVEN `the penalty the Commissioners imposed, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the tribunal thinks appropriate, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 99(4)(a) the tribunal may reduce the penalty to the amount` IS
    IF `the amount the tribunal thinks appropriate, in pounds` >= 0 AND `the amount the tribunal thinks appropriate, in pounds` <= `the penalty the Commissioners imposed, in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to reduce any penalty to such amount (including nil) as the tribunal thinks appropriate"; an amount above the penalty is not a reduction

-- Reg 99(5): "tribunal" is given its meaning by section 82 of the Value Added Tax Act 1994; a pointer.
