`reg 99(5) tribunal is given by` MEANS "section 82 of the Value Added Tax Act 1994 (meaning of tribunal)"

§§ `Regulation 100 -- Appeals against decisions of the Commissioners: procedure`

-- Reg 100(6): "conclusion date" is the date of the notice notifying the conclusions of the review.  The answer is a day on the caller's numbering.
-- src:2853 | (6) In this regulation, “conclusion date” means the date of the notice notifying the conclusions of the review.
@ref reg 100(6) (src:2853)
GIVEN `the day of the notice notifying the conclusions of the review` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `reg 100(6) the conclusion date is day` IS
    CONSIDER `the day of the notice notifying the conclusions of the review`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): no notice notifying the conclusions of the review has been given
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d

-- Reg 100(1): subject to paragraphs (2) to (4), an appeal is made before (a) the end of 30 days beginning with the date of the notice of the decision (day 29, F-PERIOD), or (b) if later, the end of the relevant period (regulation 96).  The notice of the offer of a review is given at the same time as the decision (regulation 94(2)), so the two share day 0.
-- src:2839 | (1) Subject to paragraphs (2) to (4), an appeal under regulation 99 is to be made to the tribunal before—
-- src:2840 | (a) the end of the period of 30 days beginning with the date of the notice notifying the decision to which the appeal relates; or
-- src:2841 | (b) if later, the end of the relevant period (within the meaning of regulation 96).
@ref reg 100(1) (src:2839-2841)
GIVEN `the days after the date of the notice of the decision, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` IS A NUMBER
      `reg 96(4) the relevant period ends on day` IS A NUMBER
      `a case in paragraph (2), (3) or (4) displaces paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 100(1) the appeal was made in time` IS
    IF NOT `a case in paragraph (2), (3) or (4) displaces paragraph (1)`
    THEN IF `the days after the date of the notice of the decision, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` <= 29 OR `the days after the date of the notice of the decision, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` <= `reg 96(4) the relevant period ends on day`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an appeal under regulation 99 is to be made to the tribunal before— (a) the end of the period of 30 days beginning with the date of the notice notifying the decision to which the appeal relates; or (b) if later, the end of the relevant period" [marginal (c)]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraphs (2) to (4)"; paragraph (5) lets the tribunal give permission after the end

-- Reg 100(2): where the Commissioners must review under regulation 95: no appeal until the conclusion date, and then within 30 days beginning with it (day 29).
-- src:2842 | (2) In a case where the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95—
-- src:2843 | (a) an appeal may not be made until the conclusion date; and
-- src:2844 | (b) any appeal is to be made within the period of 30 days beginning with the conclusion date.
@ref reg 100(2) (src:2842-2844)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 100(2) the appeal was made in time` IS
    IF NOT `the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a case where the Commissioners are required to undertake a review under regulation 95"
    ELSE IF `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` < 0
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an appeal may not be made until the conclusion date" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE IF `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` <= 29
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any appeal is to be made within the period of 30 days beginning with the conclusion date" [marginal (c)]

-- Reg 100(3): where a review is requested under regulation 97: no appeal unless P has been told whether a review will be undertaken; if told a review will be undertaken, none until the conclusion date and then within 30 days beginning with it; if told it will not, only with the tribunal's permission.
-- src:2845 | (3) In a case where the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97—
-- src:2846 | (a) an appeal may not be made—
-- src:2847 | (i) unless the Commissioners have notified the person concerned (“P”) as to whether or not a review will be undertaken; and
-- src:2848 | (ii) if the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken, until the conclusion date;
-- src:2849 | (b) any appeal where sub-paragraph (a)(ii) applies is to be made within the period of 30 days beginning with the conclusion date; and
-- src:2850 | (c) if the Commissioners have notified P that a review will not be undertaken, an appeal may be made only if the tribunal gives permission to appeal.
@ref reg 100(3) (src:2845-2850)
GIVEN `the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners have notified P as to whether or not a review will be undertaken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the tribunal gives permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 100(3) the appeal was made in time` IS
    IF NOT `the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In a case where the Commissioners are requested to undertake a review in accordance with regulation 97"
    ELSE IF NOT `the Commissioners have notified P as to whether or not a review will be undertaken`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an appeal may not be made— (i) unless the Commissioners have notified the person concerned (“P”) as to whether or not a review will be undertaken" [marginal (a)]
         ELSE IF `the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken`
              THEN IF `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` < 0
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) if the Commissioners have notified P that a review will be undertaken, until the conclusion date" [marginal (a)]
                   ELSE IF `the days after the conclusion date, as day 0, on which the appeal is made` <= 29
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any appeal where sub-paragraph (a)(ii) applies is to be made within the period of 30 days beginning with the conclusion date" [marginal (c)]
              ELSE IF `the tribunal gives permission to appeal`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) if the Commissioners have notified P that a review will not be undertaken, an appeal may be made only if the tribunal gives permission to appeal" [marginal (a)]

-- Reg 100(4): where regulation 98(8) applies, an appeal may be made at any time from the end of the period in regulation 98(6) to the date 30 days after the conclusion date.  A grant of a window: outside it the paragraph says nothing.  The days are on one numbering: the day the appeal is made, the day the 98(6) period ended, the conclusion date.
-- src:2851 | (4) In a case where regulation 98(8) applies, an appeal may be made at any time from the end of the period specified in regulation 98(6) to the date 30 days after the conclusion date.
@ref reg 100(4) (src:2851)
GIVEN `regulation 98(8) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the appeal is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the period specified in regulation 98(6) ended` IS A NUMBER
      `the conclusion date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 100(4) the appeal may be made` IS
    IF `regulation 98(8) applies` AND `the day the appeal is made` >= `the day on which the period specified in regulation 98(6) ended` AND `the day the appeal is made` <= `the conclusion date` + 30
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In a case where regulation 98(8) applies, an appeal may be made at any time from the end of the period specified in regulation 98(6) to the date 30 days after the conclusion date" [ruled 2026-11-05 (a) period]

-- Reg 100(5): an appeal may be made after the end of the period in paragraph (1), (2)(b), (3)(b) or (4) if the tribunal gives permission.
-- src:2852 | (5) An appeal may be made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4) if the tribunal gives permission to appeal.
@ref reg 100(5) (src:2852)
GIVEN `the appeal is made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tribunal gives permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 100(5) the appeal may be made after the end of the period` IS
    IF `the appeal is made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4)` AND `the tribunal gives permission to appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal may be made after the end of the period specified in paragraph (1), (2)(b), 3(b) or (4) if the tribunal gives permission to appeal" [marginal (a)]
